{"text": "VERITY BLUFFS HOME NURSING -- SN VISIT NOTE\nVerity Bluffs Home Nursing, 3180 Asbury Rd, Dubuque, IA 52001   ph 563-555-0127   after hours 563-555-0190\n\nPt:        ASHWORTH, ELEANOR J  (\"Nell\")       DOB 04/19/1933   Age 93\nChart #:   VB-204417         Medicare no. 4NK7-WT2-HD86\nAddress:   1466 Loras Blvd, Dubuque -- side door, 2 steps, no rail\nEpisode:   cert period 5/28/26 - 7/26/26 (Form CMS-485 signed by MD)\nVisit:     Tues 6/23/26, in 10:05, out 10:55.  RN: Thandiwe Mwangi, RN (lic. IA 148830)\nMD:        Dr. Lazlo Vukovic, Key City Heart Clinic, 563.555.0144, fax 563.555.0145\n\nAccess: Front door stays locked. Key in lockbox on the side railing, code 1933 (daughter set it; told her\nto change it). Entered with aide present.\n\nDx: chronic diastolic heart failure (ICD-10 I50.32), atrial fibrillation, type 2 diabetes,\nstage 3 chronic kidney disease, macular degeneration, hard of hearing (L worse than R).\n\nVitals: BP 148/72 sitting, HR 78 irregular, RR 18, Temp 97.9, SpO2 92% on 2L NC (88% on RA\nafter walking to the bathroom, back to 95% in 3 minutes). Wt 131.4 lb, up 3.2 lb since Friday.\nFingerstick 212 mg/dL at 10:20 (ate toast and jam at 9).\n\nReports: sleeping in the recliner x2 nights, \"can't get my breath flat.\" Denies chest pain. Pain 3/10 both knees.\nLungs: crackles both bases. Edema 2+ both ankles (was 1+ on 6/19). A&Ox3, a little forgetful about\nthe day of the week. Skin intact; heels soft. Braden Scale 16. Morse Fall Scale 55 (high).\n\nMeds reviewed against bottles. Furosemide 40 mg every morning (she calls it Lasix); apixaban 2.5 mg BID;\nmetoprolol succinate 25 mg daily; insulin glargine 14 units at bedtime. Found she skipped the water pill\nSat and Sun because of the church picnic at St. Columbkille Parish (\"didn't want to be running to the\nbathroom\"). She is a lifelong Catholic and wants Father to bring communion on weeks she can't go.\nRefill due on apixaban: Rx 6620417-02 at Asbury Road Pharmacy, (563) 555-0102.\n\nDevices:\n  Oxygen concentrator, Model EverFlo-type 5 LPM, Serial HC5-2291847, from Tri-State Oxygen & Medical Supply\n    (1-800-555-0133). Filter dusty, cleaned. Hours meter 6 214.\n  Pacemaker (dual chamber, implanted March 2019): SN: PJN508812H. Wallet card checked. Remote\n    monitor at bedside, transmitter ID TX-88014-6627, green light on.\n  Glucometer: serial GM07K31190, control solution not expired.\n  Pendant alarm worn; did not test today.\n\nCaregiver: Daughter Rosalie Koenig lives next door at 1470 Loras, cell 563-555-0168, is health care\nagent; POLST on fridge, DNR. Rosalie works nights at the casino so mornings are covered by the aide,\nMarisol Ospina, Mon/Wed/Fri 8-12 (private pay, $24/hr). Son-in-law Gus (Mr. Koenig) does the\npill box on Sundays -- he is the retired fire chief, everybody on the street knows him.\nMarisol says Mrs. Ashworth nearly fell Monday reaching for the phone.\n\nTeaching: daily weights, call if up 2-3 lb overnight or 5 lb in a week; low-salt reminders (the picnic ham);\ndo not skip the water pill. Instructed Marisol to log weights on the fridge sheet.\n\nCalled MD office 10:40, spoke to nurse. Verbal Order per Dr. Vukovic: furosemide 40 mg twice daily x 3 days,\nthen back to daily; BMP Friday 6/26; office visit July 1 2:15 pm. Read back and confirmed.\nRosalie texted re: new order and the ride on the 1st.\n\nPlan: SN 2x/wk x 3 wks then reassess (42 CFR § 484.60 care plan updated; OASIS-E not due). Goal: no\nhospitalization this episode (Medicare Part A). Next visit Fri 6/26, lab draw.\n\nElectronically signed: T. Mwangi RN  06/23/2026 11:32   visit ID V-0623-11873   mileage 6.4 mi", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "582 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Eleanor J Ashworth", "Thandiwe Mwangi", "Lazlo Vukovic", "Father", "Rosalie Koenig", "Gus Koenig", "Marisol Ospina", "T. Mwangi RN"], "companies": ["Verity Bluffs Home Nursing", "Key City Heart Clinic", "Asbury Road Pharmacy", "St. Columbkille Parish", "Tri-State Oxygen & Medical Supply"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 31358.5, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 26, "text": "VERITY BLUFFS HOME NURSING", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Verity Bluffs Home Nursing"}, {"start": 44, "end": 70, "text": "Verity Bluffs Home Nursing", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Verity Bluffs Home Nursing"}, {"start": 72, "end": 86, "text": "3180 Asbury Rd", "kind": "street", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "3180 Asbury Rd"}, {"start": 88, "end": 99, "text": "Dubuque, IA", "kind": "places", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Dubuque, IA"}, {"start": 100, "end": 105, "text": "52001", "kind": "zip", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "52001"}, {"start": 111, "end": 123, "text": "563-555-0127", "kind": "phone", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "563-555-0127"}, {"start": 138, "end": 150, "text": "563-555-0190", "kind": "phone", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "563-555-0190"}, {"start": 163, "end": 182, "text": "ASHWORTH, ELEANOR J", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Eleanor J Ashworth"}, {"start": 186, "end": 190, "text": "Nell", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Eleanor J Ashworth"}, {"start": 203, "end": 213, "text": "04/19/1933", "kind": "dob", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "04/19/1933"}, {"start": 216, "end": 222, "text": "Age 93", "kind": "age90", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Age 93"}, {"start": 234, "end": 243, "text": "VB-204417", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "VB-204417"}, {"start": 265, "end": 278, "text": "4NK7-WT2-HD86", "kind": "passport_dl", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "4NK7-WT2-HD86"}, {"start": 